  "worked_solution": "A polygon is **convex** if it has no internal angle larger than ${180}^{∘}.$ In plain words, a convex polygon has no angles pointing inwards. Otherwise, the polygon is called **concave**.\n\nA polygon is **simple** if its boundary does not intersect itself. Otherwise, the polygon is called **complex**.\n\nIn our case, the polygon is \n\n- $\\text{simple}$ since the boundary doesn't intersect itself, and\n\n- $\\text{convex}$ since it has no angles pointing inwards.",
