  "html": "<div id=\"step-q237204\" class=\"step questionWidget\" style=\"display: block;\"><div class=\"questionWidget-header\"><div class=\"questionWidget-title\">Question 6</div><div class=\"questionWidget-helpButton\">?</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-237204\"></div><div class=\"questionWidget-text\">Construct the correct description for the above polygon.  <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"14\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 2em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"15\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 2em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> The polygon is <div id=\"selectList-237204-0\" class=\"selectList\" style=\"margin: 0px 4px 2px;\"><div class=\"selectListFrameDisabled correctSelection\" id=\"selectListFrame-237204-0\" style=\"width: 74px; height: 17px; line-height: 17px;\">simple</div><div class=\"selectListOptions\" style=\"visibility: hidden; z-index: 1; left: 888px; top: 8523px;\"><div class=\"selectListOption selected\" style=\"height: 17px;\">simple</div><div class=\"selectListOption\" style=\"height: 17px;\">complex</div></div></div> and <div id=\"selectList-237204-1\" class=\"selectList\" style=\"margin: 0px 2px 2px 4px;\"><div class=\"selectListFrameDisabled correctSelection\" id=\"selectListFrame-237204-1\" style=\"width: 74px; height: 17px; line-height: 17px;\">convex</div><div class=\"selectListOptions\" style=\"visibility: hidden; z-index: 1; left: 374px; top: 8558px;\"><div class=\"selectListOption selected\" style=\"height: 17px;\">convex</div><div class=\"selectListOption\" style=\"height: 17px;\">concave</div></div></div>.<p></p></div><div class=\"questionWidget-buttonBar\"><div class=\"questionWidget-submitButton disabledButton\" style=\"display: none;\">Submit</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-spinnerFrame\"><div class=\"questionWidget-spinner\" style=\"display: block;\"></div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-result\"><div class=\"questionWidget-correctIncorrectIcon\"><img src=\"/img/correct-answer.svg\"></div><div class=\"questionWidget-correctText\">Correct</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanation\"><p>A polygon is <strong>convex</strong> if it has no internal angle larger than <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"16\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msup><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.393em;\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2218\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>180</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> In plain words, a convex polygon has no angles pointing inwards. Otherwise, the polygon is called <strong>concave</strong>.</p>\n<p>A polygon is <strong>simple</strong> if its boundary does not intersect itself. Otherwise, the polygon is called <strong>complex</strong>.</p>\n<p>In our case, the polygon is </p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"17\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle style=\"background-color: gainsboro;\"><mjx-mpadded><mjx-block style=\"width: 3.383em; margin: 0.3em 0px; position: relative;\"><mjx-rbox style=\"left: 0.3em; top: 0px; max-width: 3.383em;\"><mjx-mstyle style=\"color: blue;\"><mjx-mtext class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c73\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c69\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6D\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c70\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6C\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c65\"></mjx-c></mjx-mtext></mjx-mstyle></mjx-rbox></mjx-block></mjx-mpadded></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle mathbackground=\"Gainsboro\"><mpadded height=\"+3pt\" depth=\"+3pt\" lspace=\"3pt\" width=\"+6pt\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"blue\"><mtext>simple</mtext></mstyle></mpadded></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> since the boundary doesn't intersect itself, and </p>\n</li>\n<li><p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"18\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle style=\"background-color: gainsboro;\"><mjx-mpadded><mjx-block style=\"width: 3.6em; margin: 0.3em 0px; position: relative;\"><mjx-rbox style=\"left: 0.3em; top: 0px; max-width: 3.6em;\"><mjx-mstyle style=\"color: blue;\"><mjx-mtext class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c63\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6F\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6E\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c76\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c65\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c78\"></mjx-c></mjx-mtext></mjx-mstyle></mjx-rbox></mjx-block></mjx-mpadded></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectabl